<section image-layout="blank" id="HpA6c_QQoK" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="mE9jArafQd" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">ORIENTATION</p><p role="caption">01 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Gz95Gd4ieB" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="hTRR9Xclsr" padding="40pt 38pt 34pt" colspan="36"><labels><label variant="solid">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h1 font-size="40pt">A handover is complete when the work can move without memory</h1><p font-size="lg">An operating field guide to why the Customer Support Intake Redesign exists, how it works, what is decided, what remains uncertain, and who acts next.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>No project records were supplied.</b> Every status, metric, role, artifact version, and timeline point is a coherent example to replace or validate before operational use.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="NuPoWmnTc-" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Current phase</p><h4>Pilot validation and launch preparation</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="SzHMmWI7-y" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Overall condition</p><h4>Needs attention</h4><p font-size="sm">Core workflow works; reporting remains unresolved.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1hzosZbDXd" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Transition target</p><h4>Ownership accepted by T+10 business days</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="bwKqP8err6" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Critical path</p><p font-size="sm">Benchmark → D-04 → failed tests → launch authority.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Immediate references: D-04 on slide 6 · ownership on slide 8 · transition sequence on slide 10.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6CULvypae5" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/yUTdilxopNSUygRopkefS.png" saved-media-id="vn805b9acqvqvrc" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of modular warm-white paper blocks passing an operational-blue connector cord across a precise handover boundary, translucent tabs, graphite clips, one unresolved signal-amber gate and one field-sage accepted gate, soft directional daylight, tactile and clean, generous negative space, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="4DlaV60QDQ"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="b9YnFMnYVH" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">CONTEXT</p><p role="caption">02 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="8ugIvBovoR" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="IasL06brbM" padding="0" colspan="20"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/Ysv1R3GMHPHZrsNWPSuvk.png" saved-media-id="8rd0j22g9cnjnx0" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of three distinct paper input channels converging into one operational-blue intake tray, duplicate graphite slips set aside, a small signal-amber priority tab and field-sage acknowledgement card, soft directional daylight on warm white, precise modular arrangement, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="yHiYpSGH5a" padding="34pt 40pt 30pt" colspan="40"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>Why the project exists and what success means</h2><p>Support requests arrive through email, chat, and inconsistent web forms. Manual triage creates duplicate records, weak priority signals, and limited visibility into queue health.</p><p>The project creates one traceable intake and routing service without replacing the underlying case-management platform.</p><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="uCrEMVUDmY" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">User outcome</p><h3>≤15 minutes</h3><p font-size="sm">Acknowledgement and a valid case reference.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="64OR4heJtC" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Operational outcome</p><h3>≥90%</h3><p font-size="sm">Requests reach the correct queue without manual rerouting.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wwNQSHtvCm" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Reporting outcome</p><h3>95%</h3><p font-size="sm">Dashboard updates complete within two hours.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5Rm-cjURCj" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Control outcome</p><h3>Attributable</h3><p font-size="sm">Every priority override links to an authorized role.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Illustrative acceptance thresholds, not measured results. Non-goals: CRM replacement, staffing redesign, an automated support bot, or customer-service policy changes.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="QUsfx6IuRy"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="SIZ6XJ6kI-" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">SCOPE</p><p role="caption">03 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XIOIPwPnxs" padding="34pt 42pt 30pt 36pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>Scope is defined by deliverables, boundaries, and acceptance evidence</h2><p>Four deliverables replace a general promise to “improve support.” Each closes only when its acceptance evidence is attached.</p><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="5WL8x-ZYLR" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="top-line" colspan="30"><h3>Unified intake</h3><p font-size="sm">One validated structure for email, chat, and web. Accept when required fields, consent, duplicate checks, and acknowledgement behavior pass.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="agJmRXzYDr" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="top-line" colspan="30"><h3>Routing configuration</h3><p font-size="sm">Eight categories, priority rules, queue ownership, and supervisor overrides. Accept when representative scenarios route correctly.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Wwj31xJvva" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="top-line" colspan="30"><h3>Operational enablement</h3><p font-size="sm">Launch runbook, training, escalation path, and rollback. Accept when designated supervisors complete a rehearsal.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="zI13JFz-j2" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="top-line" colspan="30"><h3>Reporting</h3><p font-size="sm">Queue health, routing accuracy, backlog age, and overrides. Accept when refresh and reconciliation thresholds are met.</p></grid-item></grid><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="_nTgh8lLuM" colspan="27"><p role="eyebrow">Outside scope</p><p font-size="sm">CRM replacement · workforce planning · cleanup beyond 90 days · customer-facing policy changes.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="CzbJfb_6ld" colspan="33"><p role="eyebrow">Dependencies</p><p font-size="sm">Identity roles · API access · analytics export capacity · approved categories · supervisor availability · release authority.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="MEH7JnFVcB"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="uQ6HqyM0X3" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">SERVICE</p><p role="caption">04 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="RdiGtbaFJ3" padding="32pt 40pt 28pt 36pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>How a request moves through the service</h2><p>Six outputs make failures isolatable rather than one undifferentiated service problem.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="small" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="NRLMtzNEHX" colspan="20"><h4>Capture</h4><p font-size="sm">Email, chat, or web input becomes a normalized request record.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wETn7jvJpR" colspan="20"><h4>Validate</h4><p font-size="sm">Required fields, identity, consent, and duplicate signals are checked.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="zCDIKkBmod" colspan="20"><h4>Classify</h4><p font-size="sm">Rules assign one of eight categories, a priority, and confidence.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-R0KcxEiKL" colspan="20"><h4>Route</h4><p font-size="sm">Category, region, and service hours select the destination queue.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="W24dG_WUjH" colspan="20"><h4>Work</h4><p font-size="sm">The case platform records assignment, response, status, and resolution.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="oh4geCOI4k" colspan="20"><h4>Observe</h4><p font-size="sm">An export supplies queue, accuracy, backlog, and override measures.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="0R2ysYGpjc" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>Controls span the chain</h4><p font-size="sm">Identity and audit logging apply at every stage.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="fpzRsMG1Hp" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>Reporting is asynchronous</h4><p font-size="sm">Intake continues when the analytics export is delayed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="f_wcY1d1Z3" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>Failures remain recoverable</h4><p font-size="sm">Invalid or unroutable records enter the review queue; none are discarded.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="6WfMu9Es5u"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Bz73dgkyxx" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">STATUS</p><p role="caption">05 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Xjbgua7BaU" padding="30pt 40pt 26pt 36pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>Current status: core workflow works, evidence is not yet launch-complete</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="tkA6azz_EF" colspan="20"><display size="md">34/42</display><h4>Acceptance scenarios passed</h4><p font-size="sm">Five pending; three failed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gPMdpGig2i" colspan="20"><display size="md">18/24</display><h4>Designated users trained</h4><p font-size="sm">Rollback rehearsal remains open.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hOEh-Voa5S" colspan="20"><display size="md">4.5h</display><h4>Latest export</h4><p font-size="sm">Against a two-hour target.</p></grid-item></grid><table col-widths="[18,14,28]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Area</p></td><td><p>State</p></td><td><p>Evidence and consequence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Configuration</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Accepted baseline</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Validation and all eight categories configured in C-12.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Pilot</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Conditional</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">18 agents processed 120 controlled requests; routing met 90%, but the sample is not launch assurance.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Operations</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Conditional</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Runbook v0.6 exists; training and rollback evidence are incomplete.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Reporting</b></p></td><td background-color="palette-2"><p font-size="sm"><b>Blocked</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Representative benchmark and D-04 are required before launch review.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Security</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Conditional</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Review complete subject to production role confirmation.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><aside variant="warning"><p font-size="sm"><b>Critical path:</b> reporting benchmark → D-04 → close duplicate-detection, overnight-routing, and export failures → launch-readiness review.</p></aside><p role="caption">Preserve: UAT summary · pilot log · baseline C-12 · runbook v0.6 · access review.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="AICoGjJIf5"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="3LKKJ_VPTX" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">DECISIONS</p><p role="caption">06 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="97Z_v1mszy" padding="32pt 40pt 30pt 36pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>Decisions protect the project from repeating old debates</h2><p>Decision IDs remain stable when dates, owners, or evidence links change.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="xFKC0xd2vT" colspan="27"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="FNtKlI3NiP" cell-style="subtle"><labels><label variant="plain">D-01 · ACCEPTED</label></labels><h4>Eight-category taxonomy</h4><p font-size="sm">Chosen over team-specific labels. Local teams map their language into shared categories rather than create new queues.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="joNQ1aUwlB" cell-style="subtle"><labels><label variant="plain">D-02 · ACCEPTED</label></labels><h4>Supervisor-only priority overrides</h4><p font-size="sm">Improves auditability. Urgent exceptions require an available supervisor and a recorded reason.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xwGn6jZicn" cell-style="subtle"><labels><label variant="plain">D-03 · ACCEPTED</label></labels><h4>Phased rollout</h4><p font-size="sm">Two teams launch first. Delivery is slower, but exposure and rollback boundaries are measurable.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="tIPLO8WXiz" background-color="palette-2" padding="26pt 28pt" colspan="33"><p role="eyebrow">D-04 · OPEN · DRIVEN BY R-02</p><h3>Is reporting ready enough for launch?</h3><p>Choose between launching with a controlled daily export or delaying until the two-hour refresh target is met.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="BFo0TFRafh" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Accountable</p><h4>Product Owner</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="m7pnz3lHvN" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Evidence owner</p><h4>Data Lead</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="PN1Gjgvpxf" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">A-06 · Next action</p><p font-size="sm">Representative-volume benchmark by T+5.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="mcIr_0xUf5" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Decision forum</p><h4>T+6</h4></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm"><b>Launch:</b> preserves schedule, adds manual reconciliation. <b>Delay:</b> protects the reporting standard, extends dual operation.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="debrFMFUAC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="fhn3_82RMV" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">GOVERNANCE</p><p role="caption">07 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="AcCmfXZfCv" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="kcpi1wqbWF" padding="0" colspan="18"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/nZaSdDDn_VHbXTG2OvHSg.png" saved-media-id="qwjegs8wae60xvb" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of a strict vertical hierarchy of warm-white paper trays, an operational-blue decision tab at the top, graphite delivery cards below, one field-sage runbook band and a signal-amber escalation clip, connected by a single precise cord, soft directional daylight, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="WnbBCeWxWB" padding="32pt 38pt 28pt" colspan="42"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>Ways of working: one hierarchy of truth and explicit escalation</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="ApRQ0RmsfQ" padding="9pt 0"><h4>Decision log</h4><p font-size="sm">Authoritative for accepted choices, rationale, consequences, and superseded decisions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7z_9GPOqe9" padding="9pt 0"><h4>Delivery board</h4><p font-size="sm">Authoritative for active owner, status, dependency, and target sequence.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="o2yWN7AFps" padding="9pt 0"><h4>Runbook</h4><p font-size="sm">Authoritative for launch, rollback, incident response, and routine operation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ApcpDetCKz" padding="9pt 0"><h4>Chat and meetings</h4><p font-size="sm">Coordination only. A decision is not accepted until recorded in the log.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="UVSgVRVNvo" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Cadence and change control</h4><p font-size="sm">Weekly 30-minute decision forum; twice-weekly delivery review; daily asynchronous update from T+5 through stabilization. Record a proposal for changes to acceptance, data, launch sequence, or more than two business days.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UlOLwgf6TC" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Escalation and completion</h4><p font-size="sm">Escalate access gaps, rehearsal queue age above five minutes, reporting above four hours, or missing authority. Work is done when evidence is attached, the runbook is updated, and the receiver accepts it.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ryCYWX5sJN"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="OzvTLJ-7kz" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">OWNERSHIP</p><p role="caption">08 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="T6F5vQDvSy" padding="30pt 40pt 26pt 36pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>Ownership follows outcomes, systems, and operating continuity</h2><p>Replace role labels with verified people and deputies before handover acceptance.</p><table col-widths="[20,14,26]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Role</p></td><td><p>Stance</p></td><td><p>Owned outcome or continuity duty</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="palette-3"><p font-size="sm"><b>Product Owner</b></p></td><td background-color="palette-3"><p font-size="sm"><b>Accountable</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Outcomes, scope, thresholds, launch authority, and D-04.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Incoming Project Manager</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Responsible · coordinating</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Integrated plan, RAID record, decision forum, evidence index, and acceptance.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Outgoing Project Manager</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Responsible to T+10</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Context transfer, reconciliation, introductions, and historical clarification.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Technical Lead</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Responsible</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Configuration, routing, integrations, release execution, and rollback.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Operations Lead</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Responsible</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Training, supervisor readiness, launch coverage, and adoption.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Data Lead</b></p></td><td background-color="palette-2"><p font-size="sm"><b>Responsible · A-06</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Export benchmark, dashboard reconciliation, monitoring, and reporting fallback.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Security Reviewer</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Consulted</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Production roles, audit controls, and exception review.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Support Supervisors</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Consulted · informed</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Workflow validation, override use, and frontline feedback.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><aside variant="success"><p font-size="sm"><b>Continuity gate:</b> named deputies for Product Owner, Technical Lead, and Operations Lead; production and reporting access for the incoming team; accepted ownership of every recurring meeting, dashboard, and escalation duty.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ihpoJXSle5"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="esy5xYVPDC" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">ASSURANCE</p><p role="caption">09 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="h1nGvuhhWG" padding="30pt 40pt 26pt 36pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>Risks, issue, and open questions converge on launch confidence</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="P19S0QWjCU" colspan="25"><h3>Risk register</h3><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small"><grid-item id="Ax26GnqP3Z" cell-style="subtle"><h4>R-01 · Adoption · Medium / high</h4><p font-size="sm">Trigger: &gt;20% manual rerouting. Operations Lead responds with category coaching and targeted rule review.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="mzOs4Ftqsc" cell-style="subtle"><h4>R-03 · Taxonomy drift · Medium / medium</h4><p font-size="sm">Trigger: &gt;10% uncategorized work. Product Owner reviews weekly; local categories are not permitted.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="kS4XCkoIG6" cell-style="subtle"><h4>R-04 · API rate limiting · Low / high</h4><p font-size="sm">Trigger: queue age above five minutes. Technical Lead enables throttling and controlled replay.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="dgPraEcRpW" colspan="35"><h3>Reporting is the launch-confidence chain</h3><smart-layout variant="staircase" cell-size="10"><smart-layout-item><h4>Reporting dependency</h4><p>The asynchronous export supplies operational measures.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>R-02 · High / high</h4><p>Triggered when refresh exceeds two hours.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>I-01 · Active issue</h4><p>Latest representative export completed in 4.5 hours.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>A-06 · Response</h4><p>Benchmark volume and prepare a controlled daily fallback.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>D-04 · Open</h4><p>Launch with fallback or delay for the two-hour standard.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout></grid-item></grid><p role="eyebrow">Open questions that must close</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ko0leulqtK" colspan="15"><p font-size="sm">Can the export meet target at representative volume by T+5?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="4omIzh-R0b" colspan="15"><p font-size="sm">Is a daily fallback acceptable for the first rollout group?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="VPF943VSOV" colspan="15"><p font-size="sm">What minimum pilot sample authorizes expansion?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="g4PocMenFj" colspan="15"><p font-size="sm">Who approves an emergency override when the supervisor is unavailable?</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ZEMMote33n"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="vdCB7DPQsK" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">TRANSITION</p><p role="caption">10 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZWjPsmm7y_" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="y9Szb4QtSN" padding="0" colspan="16"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/LLYjFJyvgygrUCJJQBkHn.png" saved-media-id="f87oz7zul1b2xi2" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of a sequence of modular warm-white paper blocks connected across a thirty-day transition path, operational-blue cord passing through field-sage accepted gates with one signal-amber decision gate, graphite clips and translucent tabs, soft directional daylight, precise and calm, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="tnKEbNr8Vj" padding="30pt 38pt 26pt" colspan="44"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2>The next 30 days turn transferred knowledge into accepted ownership</h2><p font-size="sm">T+0 is the formal start of handover. Relative markers begin when handover is formally accepted.</p><table col-widths="[9,16,35]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>When</p></td><td><p>Owner</p></td><td><p>Required result</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="accent"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+1</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Incoming PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Confirm owners, deputies, artifact locations, invitations, and access requests.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>T+3</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Incoming PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Walk the system path, reconcile the delivery board, and record contradictions.</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="palette-2"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+5</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Data + Operations</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Complete A-06 benchmark, training, and rollback rehearsal.</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="palette-2"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+6</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Product Owner</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Decide D-04 from benchmark evidence and record the consequence.</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="palette-3"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+10</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Product Owner + PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Review failed tests, roles, fallback, and authority; accept or extend handover.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>T+15</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Technical + Operations</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Execute the first rollout only if entry criteria are met.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>T+30</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Product Owner + PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Review stability, adoption, unresolved risks, and temporary controls.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><aside variant="success"><p font-size="sm"><b>Acceptance test:</b> the incoming owner can explain the purpose, locate authoritative evidence, identify who can decide, describe rollback, and name the next three actions without help.</p></aside><p role="caption">Anything that still depends on private memory becomes a documented action, not an assumption.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>